<PageLayout
  title="Request a Speaker | Silver Lining of Hope"
  description="Book Silver Lining of Hope speakers for agencies, classrooms, and community groups: hidden homicides, missing person advocacy, and victims' rights."
  heading="Request a speaker"
  intro="First-hand experience, presented with care — not true-crime entertainment."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Get involved', href: '/get-involved' },
    { label: 'Request a speaker', href: '/get-involved/request-a-speaker' },
  ]}
>
  <div class="container--narrow section prose">
    <h2>Topics we speak on</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>From daughter to advocate</strong> — how seven months of independent research helped reopen a homicide case, and what it revealed about the system. Our founder's story, told with purpose.</li>
      <li><strong>Hidden homicides</strong> — deaths misclassified as accidents or overdoses: warning signs, family experiences, and what better review would look like.</li>
      <li><strong>The missing persons data gap</strong> — what building <a href="/programs/the-missing-link">The Missing Link</a> is teaching us about who falls out of the databases and why.</li>
      <li><strong>Trauma-informed advocacy</strong> — how to work with grieving and traumatized families, for students, victim advocates, and service professionals.</li>
      <li><strong>Victims' rights legislation in Indiana</strong> — Dom &amp; Davion's Law, Hailey's Law, and how communities move bills.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who we speak to</h2>
    <p>
      Law enforcement trainings, criminal justice and social work classrooms,
      victim services organizations, civic groups, and conferences. Talks are
      free for community groups; honoraria from funded organizations go
      entirely to <a href="/donate">the mission</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Make a request</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/about/contact">Contact us</a> with your organization, likely
      audience and size, preferred dates, and which topic fits. We'll respond
      within a few days.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
